      "repair_reason": "- [P1] No automated code repair is indicated; the blocker is refreshed contributor proof for the live head plus maintainer review of the synchronization path.; Cleared: The diff only changes a private Swift synchronization helper and call sites; it does not alter dependencies, secrets, CI, packaging metadata, or external code execution. (sha=3224464183c6e0db7c1ea85d9b47d77475a0a9f9)",
      "review_summary": "The PR replaces `CanonicalMessageProofHub`'s closure helper with explicit lock/unlock calls in `ChatTranscriptCache.cancelCommand` so actor-isolated SQLite work stays in the actor body while preserving the proof/commit lock window.\n\nPR surface: Other +5. Total +5 across 1 file.\n\nReproducibility: yes. in source-backed form: current main still passes actor-isolated SQLite work through the synchronous `withProofDecision` closure inside `cancelCommand`. I did not run Swift 6.2 in this read-only review.",
